Revolut has four different account and card tiers, including Revolut Standard, Revolut Plus, Revolut Premium, and Revolut Metal. The following are some of the best features for each account type:

Revolut pricing plans comparison (as of the time of writing).

To see the detailed list of Revolut pricing plans’ features, check the image above. Below is a brief description of each pricing plan.

### Standard Account [...] You can withdraw cash from an ATM using your Revolut card for free, up to the limits of your plan; after that, Revolut will charge a fee.

The fee-free limits on Revolut plans for ATM withdrawals are as follows:

 Standard: €200, or 5 ATM withdrawals per month (whatever comes first);
 Plus: €200 per month;
 Premium: €400 per month;
 Metal: €800 per month.

Beyond these limits, you will pay a 2% fee on all money withdrawn, with a minimum fee of €1 per withdrawal. [...] 1. Commission fees: Revolut charges a commission per trade, outside the monthly allowance of one free trade for Standard, three for Plus, five for Premium, and ten for Metal plans. The commission fee is either 0.25% of the order amount or the minimum country-specific fee, whichever is higher, and will be charged in USD using the FX rate once the order is received;
2. Custody fees: 0.12% / 12 bps (on an annual basis) of the market value of your assets, charged monthly;
